<title>PORTUGAL: ICSG sees modest copper supply surplus in 1997.</title>
<headline>ICSG sees modest copper supply surplus in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Copper Study Group (ICSG) said it forecast a modest surplus of copper supplies in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;On the basis of forecasts supplied by member nations, the ICSG expects a modest supply surplus in 1997. However, this forecast assumes that plants work at planned levels for the entire year,&quot; the ICSG said after its annual meeting in Lisbon.</p>
<p>The ICSG said in a statement the copper market in 1996 was roughly in balance.</p>
<p>The statement gave no figures.</p>
<p>Russia had joined the ICSG, the statement added.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
